+## 7. Central Registry Architecture (4 Distinct Linked Tables & Component-Specific Provenance)
+
+To maintain a single auditable inventory without conflating distinct component types, the central registry consists of **four distinct, linked tables** (`7.2.A` Skills, `7.2.B` Plugins & Marketplaces, `7.2.C` MCP Servers, `7.2.D` Executable Tools), backed by a component-specific provenance model.
+
+### 7.1 Required Registry Fields & Component-Specific Provenance Model
+
+Because `skills-lock.json` v2 `computedHash` ([`vercel-labs/skills`](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills)) is defined specifically over a **Skill directory** (`UTF-8` sorted relative paths excluding `metadata.json`, `.git`, `__pycache__`, `__pypackages__`, with `CRLF -> LF` normalization and `SHA256(path + "␀" + decimal_byte_len + "␀" + content)`), it **must not** be used as a universal substitute for Git commit SHAs, plugin archive digests, or binary digests. Every registry entry records:
+1. `canonical_name` (kebab-case identifier matching directory/slug)
+2. `kind` (`skill` | `plugin` | `mcp_server` | `executable_tool`)
+3. `functional_domain` (`story` | `visual` | `videolane` | `audio` | `maps` | `blender_legacy` | `assembly` | `cloud_cost` | `qa_governance`)
+4. `security_profile` (`SP-1`..`SP-6`, defined in Section 9.1) and `validation_profile` (`VP-1`..`VP-6`, defined in Section 8.1)
+5. `source_repository` (canonical URL or `vano1919/explainer-engine`)
+6. **Component-Specific Provenance Fields:**
+   - `source_git_sha_40`: Full 40-character Git commit SHA (or `NOT_VERIFIED_40CHAR (<7-char>)` prior to local clone)
+   - `release_tag_or_version`: SemVer release tag (`v2.0.0`, `v1.4.0`, `v3.10.1`, `v1.5.25`) or `N/A`
+   - `skill_folder_computed_hash`: `skills-lock.json` v2 `computedHash` (required when `kind == "skill"` and unpacked locally; `N/A` for non-skill kinds)
+   - `package_archive_sha256`: Tarball/zip SHA-256 or npm SHA-512 integrity hash (required when `kind == "plugin"` or packaged archive)
+   - `binary_or_image_digest`: Exact binary version constraint + local binary SHA-256 / container digest (for `kind in {"mcp_server", "executable_tool"}`)
+   - `first_party_repo_revision`: Local Git commit SHA (`eb80e4434ea120f48cb9aea094ebd7b2b423d8f0`) for tracked first-party files
+7. `license_and_attribution` (SPDX identifier + copyright notice path)
+8. `required_tools` (linked `executable_tool` IDs) and `required_mcp_servers` (linked `mcp_server` IDs)
+9. `claude_code_compatibility` (minimum Claude Code version, frontmatter extensions, cloud vs. local session support)
+10. `lifecycle_state` (one of the 9 states in Section 6.2), `owner_approval`, and `update_policy` (`pinned-manual-review`)
+
