+## 8. Risk-Based Zero-Cost Validation Strategy & Argon Operational Guardrails
+
+### 8.1 Tiered Validation Profiles (`VP-1` through `VP-6`)
+
+Instead of a rigid one-size-fits-all checklist that either over-burdens pure Markdown edits or under-tests executable code and visual media, validation is tiered by component risk:
+
+| Profile | Target Component Type | Mandatory `$0.00` Local Validation Gates Before `INSTALLED` | Mandatory Post-Install / Production Verification (`PRODUCTION VALIDATED`) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **`VP-1`** | **Pure Markdown Skill / Rule** (`.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, `.claude/rules/*.md`, `0` scripts) | 1. YAML frontmatter lint (`name` matches dir & `^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$`, not `synced`/`anthropic-skills`; `description <= 1024` chars; body `< 500` lines / `< 5,000` tokens).<br>2. `python -m explainer_engine.docs_lint` (`0 finding(s)`).<br>3. `pytest tests/unit/test_agent_governance.py tests/unit/test_t3_agent_skill_banners.py`.<br>4. Static positive/negative trigger phrase matrix (`>= 5` positive, `>= 5` negative near-miss prompts) + startup description token budget check. | Verify on 1 representative dry-run task that Claude loads references progressively without breaking `stage_guard` or `no_names`. |
+| **`VP-2`** | **Skill + Local CLI / Python Script** (`scripts/*.py`, `explainer_engine/**`, `tools/render_tools/**`) | All `VP-1` gates **plus**:<br>1. Static AST/grep audit (`0` `shell=True`, `0` network sockets, `0` `sys.modules` leaks).<br>2. `--help` and `--dry-run` execution test in isolated `tmp_path` verifying `0` source files mutated.<br>3. Schema validation of JSON outputs against `explainer_engine/core/contracts.py` (`episode_timing/1` & `/2`, `production_script/4`).<br>4. Frame-exact math verification (`24fps` integer frame counts; zero millisecond drift). | **Mandatory Eye + Ear Gate (Argon Lesson):** Synthetic unit tests never suffice for media scripts. Must render a real vertical-slice contact sheet + waveform check and pass independent fresh-context critic review (`script-critic` / `youtube-viewer-critic`) + Owner visual sign-off. |
+| **`VP-3`** | **Local Stdio MCP Server** (`.mcp.json` -> local process) | All `VP-2` gates **plus**:<br>1. `claude plugin validate` / `.mcp.json` schema check (`v2.1.281+`).<br>2. `tools/list` token footprint check (`<= 15` default tools).<br>3. Verify `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` matcher intercepts both `mcp__<server>__.*` and `mcp__plugin_<plugin>_<server>__.*` (`exit 2` on mutating/unapproved calls in `test_governance_hooks.py`). | Verify clean subprocess teardown on `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` with zero orphaned background processes. |
+| **`VP-4`** | **Remote HTTP MCP / External API Connector** (`mcp__ElevenLabs`, `hyperstack-docs-mcp`) | 1. Endpoint TLS & read-only capability audit.<br>2. Synthetic `PreToolUse` hook tests in `tests/unit/test_governance_hooks.py` & `tests/unit/test_money_path_fences.py` proving unapproved calls exit `2` (`$0.00` offline test).<br>3. Verify cloud-session fallback behavior. | Live call permitted **only** when explicitly budgeted in `config/spend_caps.json` and approved by Owner for an active episode gate. |
+| **`VP-5`** | **Full Claude Plugin Package** (`.claude-plugin/plugin.json`) | All `VP-1..VP-3` gates for bundled components **plus**:<br>1. Inspect `plugin.json`, `hooks/hooks.json`, `monitors`, `mods`, and `bin/` directory (`0` unauthorized `bin/` executables, `0` auto-starting `monitors`, `0` `mods`).<br>2. Confirm no security-critical subagent relies on ignored plugin frontmatter (`hooks`, `mcpServers`, `permissionMode`).<br>3. Verify `package_archive_sha256` and `source_git_sha_40`. | Verify in local `claude --plugin-dir` test session before project registration; document that `.claude/settings.json` plugins do not load in cloud sessions. |
+| **`VP-6`** | **Paid Cloud GPU / Billable Provider Tool** (`RunPod`, `Modal`, `Hyperstack`, `ElevenLabs` generation) | All `VP-2` & `VP-4` gates **plus**:<br>1. Dual-layer refusal test: both `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` hook (`explainer_engine.cloud.hooks`) **and** worker entrypoint (`cheapest.py` / `paid_offer/1` `CH-01..CH-07`) must refuse unapproved runs (`$0.00` mock test).<br>2. Verify `config/spend_caps.json` cap > `$0` (`modal` / `hyperstack` general episode lines are currently `$0` / unset and therefore hard-blocked). | Requires per-run `paid_offer/1` card, free-credit check, watchdog attachment (`paid-run-watchdog`), and explicit Owner `cmsg_*` approval. |
+
+### 8.2 Mandatory Argon Operational Guardrails (`AG-01`–`AG-06`)
+
+Derived directly from the repository's Argon/Opus/ChatGPT incident history (`docs/wip/argon_2026-11-14/09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md`, `24_OPUS_VISUAL_CHECK_MAPS_S8.md`, `36_CHATGPT_REVIEW_OF_PLAN_R1.md`, `37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md`, `INCIDENT_JOURNAL_argon_loop.md`), every implementation agent and skill must obey six non-negotiable engineering rules:
+- **`AG-01` (No `sys.modules` Leaks in Tests):** Never mutate `sys.modules[...]` directly or call private `monkeypatch._undo` in tests; always use `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, name, fake)` so full-suite `pytest` runs never poison downstream modules (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 1).
+- **`AG-02` (No Test-Accommodation Fallbacks in Production Code):** Never add production fallback branches (such as appending insert audio at the end of an unsplit read when timestamps are missing) just to make a stubbed unit test pass (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 2).
+- **`AG-03` (Generated Standards & `docs_lint` Sync):** Whenever `explainer_engine/standards/sourced_rules.json` is edited, immediately run `python -m explainer_engine.standards.sourced_rules write` and `python -m explainer_engine.docs_lint` (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 3).
+- **`AG-04` (Schema Immutability During Data/Episode Fixes):** Never weaken or loosen a JSON Schema in `explainer_engine/schemas/` (e.g., permitting `motion_imitation` on `video` shots) to silence a validation error in an episode data file; fix the episode data (`37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md` R1).
+- **`AG-05` (Preserve JSON Formatting & Avoid Bulk Template Slop):** Never run whole-file `json.dumps(..., indent=2)` rewrites that create 30,000-line diffs across `production_script.json`, and never substitute generic template loops for shot-specific creative direction (`INCIDENT_JOURNAL_argon_loop.md` 15:00 & 19:30).
+- **`AG-06` (Synthetic Tests != Visual Quality):** Passing `pytest` checks structural invariants only. Any change affecting maps, snow/steam/fire overlays, 2.5D parallax, framing, or transitions must be verified by inspecting rendered multi-frame contact sheets (`look.py` / `37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md` V1–V6) before claiming completion.
