+## 9. Component-Specific Security Profiles & $0 Cost Architecture
+
+### 9.1 Resolving the Hook-as-Sandbox Fallacy (`SP-1` through `SP-6`)
+
+**Critical Security Distinction:** Claude Code `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` hooks inspect the **tool invocation envelope** (tool name and JSON arguments) before execution. Once a `PreToolUse` hook exits `0` to allow a `Bash` command, Python script, or local MCP tool call, **hooks provide zero OS-level filesystem, network, environment-variable, or child-process sandboxing**. Furthermore, per [Claude Code Plugin Security Documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security), third-party plugins have **five distinct code-execution surfaces**:
+1. `hooks/hooks.json` lifecycle shell commands
+2. `monitors` (background shell processes started automatically at session start, plugin reload, or skill activation)
+3. `mods` (JavaScript running inside Claude Code's own process with full user permissions)
+4. `mcpServers` (local stdio or remote HTTP servers whose tools are prefixed `mcp__plugin_<plugin-name>_<server-name>__<tool>`, which bypasses bare `mcp__<server>__.*` hook matchers!)
+5. `bin/` directory (executables automatically prepended to the `Bash` tool's `PATH` when the plugin is enabled!)
+
+Accordingly, every component is bound to one of six explicit **Security Profiles**:
+
+| Security Profile | Component Scope | Allowed Execution Surface | Mandatory Containment & Enforcement Controls |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **`SP-1` — Pure Instruction Skill** | `.claude/skills/<name>/` containing only `.md` and static `.json` templates | Prompt context only (`0` executable files) | Verify `find <skill_dir> -type f ! -name '*.md' ! -name '*.json'` is empty; zero runtime privilege risk. |
+| **`SP-2` — Skill + Local Deterministic Script** | `.claude/skills/<name>/scripts/*.py` or `explainer_engine/**` CLI tools | Local Python 3.10+ stdlib + approved local binaries (`ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`) | 1. Static AST audit bans `urllib`, `requests`, `httpx`, `socket`, `subprocess(..., shell=True)`, and reads of `.env` / `vault.json` / `~/.ssh` / `~/.aws`.<br>2. Scripts must take explicit input/output paths, refuse overwriting inputs, and support `--dry-run`. |
+| **`SP-3` — Local Stdio MCP Server** | `.mcp.json` stdio process | Persistent local child process speaking JSON-RPC over stdio | 1. Must be launched with a sanitized environment (`env -i PATH=... HOME=...`, stripping cloud API keys).<br>2. `.claude/settings.json` must register `PreToolUse` matchers for **both** `mcp__<server>__.*` and `mcp__plugin_.*_<server>__.*`. |
+| **`SP-4` — Remote HTTP MCP Server** | `.mcp.json` or Claude Connector HTTP endpoint | Outbound HTTPS JSON-RPC to named vendor domain | 1. Read-only endpoints (`hyperstack-docs-mcp`) allowed at `$0`.<br>2. Mixed read/write connectors (`mcp__ElevenLabs`, `hyperstack-console-mcp`) require a dedicated Python `PreToolUse` hook in `.claude/settings.json` that allowlists read-only tools and blocks mutating/billable tools unless all repository gates pass. |
+| **`SP-5` — Full Claude Plugin Package** | `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Multi-component bundle | 1. **Hard ban** on third-party plugins containing `mods`, `monitors`, or `bin/` executables unless each binary/script passes full `SP-2` line-by-line review.<br>2. Never place security-critical subagents inside a plugin (Claude Code strips `hooks`, `mcpServers`, and `permissionMode` from plugin subagents).<br>3. Prefer vendoring vetted `SKILL.md` + `references/` (`--copy`) under `.claude/skills/` (`SP-1`/`SP-2`) over enabling full third-party plugins. |
+| **`SP-6` — Billable Cloud / GPU / Paid API Tool** | `explainer_engine/cloud/*`, `modal`, `runpod`, `hyperstack`, paid `ElevenLabs` / `Gemini` / `BFL` / `fal` | External billable infrastructure | **Dual-Key Defense in Depth:** Guarded simultaneously by (a) `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` hook (`explainer_engine.cloud.hooks` / `explainer_engine.standards.hook`) **and** (b) in-code worker preflight (`cheapest.py` `CH-01..CH-07`, `paid_offer/1`, `spend_caps.json`, and 60-minute `governance ok` creator-word verification). |
+
+### 9.2 Binding $0 Cost & Operational Invariants
+
+1. **Zero Paid Calls Without Dual Gates (`SP-6`):** No Skill, Subagent, Plugin, or MCP server may initiate any paid API or GPU call without passing both the `PreToolUse` hook and the in-code `spend_caps.json` / `paid_offer/1` preflight with explicit Owner approval.
+2. **No Automatic Installation or Auto-Update:** `npx skills update`, `/plugin update`, or unpinned `git pull` inside `.claude/` are forbidden in automated flows. All third-party skills/plugins are copied (`--copy`) after review and pinned by `source_git_sha_40` + component-specific integrity hash.
+3. **Telemetry & Credential Hygiene:** Set `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1` and `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` whenever running third-party discovery CLIs (`npx skills`), and never pass `.env`, `vault.json`, or API keys to external skill scripts or local stdio MCP servers.
