+## 6.9 Cross-Cutting Global Policy: Claude Code Native Agent, Skill, Tool & Plugin Ecosystem (`DEC-2026-11-17-02` — Proposed)
+
+Explainer Engine targets **Claude Code** ([official documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills)) as its primary development and episode-orchestration environment. The complete architecture, 10-dimension content-based discovery methodology, candidate evaluations ([`wuwangzhang1216/DirectorSKILL`](https://github.com/wuwangzhang1216/DirectorSKILL), [`RobLe3/cc-blender-skill`](https://github.com/RobLe3/cc-blender-skill), `zq940222/blender-mcp-skill`, [`kajisho5/ffmpeg-skill`](https://github.com/kajisho5/ffmpeg-skill), [`anthropics/claude-plugins-official`](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official), [`vercel-labs/skills`](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills), and [`agentskills.io/specification`](https://agentskills.io/specification)), 14-subagent assessment, 9-stage lifecycle state machine, 4-table linked registry, security profiles (`SP-1..SP-6`), risk-based validation profiles (`VP-1..VP-6`), and Argon guardrails (`AG-01..AG-06`) are specified in [CLAUDE_CODE_NATIVE_ECOSYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md](CLAUDE_CODE_NATIVE_ECOSYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md).
+
+Key cross-cutting invariants applying to every phase without altering `P1.3` (`Read-only Production State and dependency snapshot`) or phase ordering:
+1. **Strict Separation of Responsibilities:** `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/rules/*.md` hold concise project invariants and safety/cost fences; `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` holds on-demand procedural workflows using progressive disclosure (`< 500` lines / `< 5,000` tokens); `.claude/agents/*.md` preserves the `config/model_routing.json` lock (`orchestrator` and `lora-coordinator` as sole spawners; `script-critic`, `lora-checkpoint-judge`, and pending `youtube-viewer-critic` as read-only Opus critics; writer/operator roles as in-process stage pages; `multi-agent-analysis` guarded by `"only on the creator's word (part 5)"`); `.claude/settings.json` hooks enforce deterministic pre/post policy checks; and executable Tools / MCP servers provide deterministic execution.
+2. **Mandatory 10-Dimension Content-Based & Plugin Discovery:** Every new capability request across Phases 1–8 must follow the Tool-First / Skill-First decision matrix (Cases A–D) and inspect the actual contents of `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `scripts/`, `bin/`, `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`, `hooks/hooks.json`, `monitors`, `mods`, `.mcp.json`, `LICENSE`, tests/evals, and open issues across official Anthropic, vendor, and vetted community sources. Never adopt a Skill, Plugin, or MCP server by title or star count alone.
+3. **9-Stage Governance, Component-Specific Provenance & Tiered Security/Validation:** Every external Skill, Plugin, or MCP candidate progresses through `DISCOVERED -> CONTENT REVIEWED -> TECHNICALLY EVALUATED -> SECURITY / LICENSE REVIEWED -> SANDBOX VALIDATED -> OWNER APPROVED -> INSTALLED -> PRODUCTION VALIDATED -> UPDATE / DEPRECATION REVIEW`, tracked across the 4-table registry (`Skills`, `Plugins`, `MCP Servers`, `Executable Tools`) with component-specific provenance hashes, security profiles (`SP-1..SP-6`), risk-based `$0.00` validation profiles (`VP-1..VP-6`), and Argon guardrails (`AG-01..AG-06`).
